WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.345
Lesson 0.3.

00:00:02.345 --> 00:00:04.990
Buying your first crypto without overpaying.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.989
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:06.989 --> 00:00:08.988
able to fund your account and make a

00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:10.825
first purchase at a sensible cost.

00:00:12.125 --> 00:00:13.415
Here's the plan.

00:00:13.415 --> 00:00:15.100
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.815
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:19.340
Then, your checklist.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.502
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:22.802 --> 00:00:24.877
(a price markup) plus a

00:00:24.877 --> 00:00:27.655
fee. network fees, called "gas") and some USDC

00:00:27.655 --> 00:00:30.911
(a dollar stablecoin for practice). First, Deposit

00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:34.238
your money, usually by bank transfer (cheapest) or card

00:00:34.238 --> 00:00:37.746
(fastest, most expensive). Next, Instant buy / convert

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:39.980
buttons are simple but often include a

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.801
spread. Then, the trading screen ("advanced"

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.005
or "spot trading") uses an order

00:00:45.005 --> 00:00:47.576
book:. Also, Market order: buy now

00:00:47.576 --> 00:00:49.716
at the best available price.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.566
On top of that, Limit

00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:53.910
order: buy only at your chosen

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.101
price or better. It often

00:00:56.101 --> 00:00:58.521
has a lower fee ("maker" fee).

00:00:59.821 --> 00:01:02.764
And finally, what to buy first for this program:

00:01:02.764 --> 00:01:04.746
a little ETH (you need it to pay.

00:01:06.046 --> 00:01:11.471
Buying $500 of ETH: Same ETH, ~$18 difference.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.586
Your exchange's fee page has the real numbers.

00:01:14.586 --> 00:01:20.931
Card + instant buy, ~3.99%, ~$19.95.

00:01:20.931 --> 00:01:26.856
Bank transfer + limit order, ~0.4%, ~$2.00.

00:01:28.156 --> 00:01:29.616
Here's your checklist.

00:01:29.616 --> 00:01:31.151
Do it now, for real.

00:01:31.151 --> 00:01:34.876
First, Deposited by the cheapest method available to me.

00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:37.679
Next, Bought a small amount of ETH

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:40.701
(for gas) and USDC (for practice).

00:01:40.701 --> 00:01:43.536
Then, Tried a limit order on the trading screen.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.169
And finally, Saved a record: date, amount,

00:01:46.169 --> 00:01:48.741
price, fees (you'll need records for tax).

00:01:50.041 --> 00:01:51.251
Question 1.

00:01:51.251 --> 00:01:53.069
Why keep a little ETH even

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:55.156
if you mostly want stablecoins?

00:01:59.576 --> 00:02:02.803
The answer: You need ETH to pay network fees

00:02:02.803 --> 00:02:06.531
(gas) on Ethereum and most of its low-cost networks.

00:02:07.831 --> 00:02:09.076
Question 2.

00:02:09.076 --> 00:02:10.808
Market or limit order: which

00:02:10.808 --> 00:02:12.421
controls the price you pay?

00:02:16.841 --> 00:02:18.466
The answer: A limit order.

00:02:19.766 --> 00:02:21.036
Question 3.

00:02:21.036 --> 00:02:22.701
Why keep records from day one?

00:02:27.121 --> 00:02:30.151
The answer: Most countries tax crypto gains.

00:02:30.151 --> 00:02:32.216
Records of dates, amounts, prices

00:02:32.216 --> 00:02:34.341
and fees make that straightforward.

00:02:35.641 --> 00:02:36.886
Let's recap.

00:02:36.886 --> 00:02:39.901
Deposit your money, usually by bank transfer

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:43.216
(cheapest) or card (fastest, most expensive).

00:02:43.216 --> 00:02:45.298
Instant buy / convert buttons are

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:47.681
simple but often include a spread.

00:02:47.681 --> 00:02:50.050
The trading screen ("advanced" or "spot

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.126
trading") uses an order book:.

00:02:52.126 --> 00:02:55.201
Market order: buy now at the best available price.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:59.016
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:02:59.016 --> 00:03:02.146
Next up, Lesson 0.4: Exchange account vs

00:03:02.146 --> 00:03:04.971
your own wallet: who holds the keys?.
